                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "conditionals_without_if",
                    "title": "Conditionals without if",
                    "explanation": "En negociaciones y textos formales se usan alternativas a «if»:\n- «provided (that)», «providing», «as long as»: siempre que.\n- «on condition that»: con la condición de que.\n- «unless»: a menos que.\n- «supposing», «assuming»: suponiendo que.\n- «otherwise»: si no, de lo contrario.\n- «but for» + nombre: de no ser por: «But for your pilot, we'd never have got this far.»\n\nCondicionales con inversión (más formales, sin «if»):\n- «Should he make an offer…» (= «If he makes an offer»)\n- «Were I in your position…» (= «If I were…»)\n- «Had I known…» (= «If I had known…»)",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Expresión",
                        "Significado",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "provided (that) / as long as",
                          "siempre que",
                          "I'll invest, provided that I get a seat on the board."
                        ],
                        [
                          "on condition that",
                          "con la condición de que",
                          "…on condition that the studio grows by thirty percent."
                        ],
                        [
                          "unless",
                          "a menos que",
                          "Unless something drastic happened, I wouldn't pull out."
                        ],
                        [
                          "supposing / assuming",
                          "suponiendo que",
                          "Supposing we don't reach thirty percent?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "otherwise",
                          "si no, de lo contrario",
                          "Go. Otherwise, you'll always wonder."
                        ],
                        [
                          "but for + nombre",
                          "de no ser por",
                          "But for your pilot, we'd never have got this far."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Should / Were / Had + sujeto",
                          "condicional formal con inversión",
                          "Should he make an offer, tell me first."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm prepared to invest, provided that I get a seat on the board.",
                      "As long as we keep creative control, that seems fair.",
                      "But for your pilot project, we'd never have got this far.",
                      "Should he make an offer, though, tell me first."
                    ]
                  }
                },
